@startuml Walker and validating

!pragma teoz true

title Files gate and validator (details of the Import chain diagram)

control "groups\n(any source)" as Groups
control "gate" as Gate
box identify #LightSkyBlue
control "read\n(exiftool, classify,\nmerge, fingerprint)" as Exif
control "validate" as Validator
control "show\n(sizes, cheap preview)" as Transcode
end box
database "DB (gorm)" as DB

== gate ==

note over Groups: the walk wrote the rows (new? size/mtime changed?)\nbefore the groupers; unchanged rows are not written
Groups -> Gate: a whole asset: its files (changed?) and\nthe files gone for the library; no main file yet
activate Gate
opt Missing
    Gate -> DB: the model's Gone (see the end of the walk)
end
alt changed (stat, role)
    Gate -> Exif: group
else unchanged
    Gate -> DB: item of the group done?\n(Visible, Waiting, Ready; Rework)
    alt done
        Gate ->x Gate: drop (no exif, no work)
    else not done (New, Dirty, Rework, interrupted)
        Gate -> Exif: group
    end
end
deactivate Gate

Exif -> Validator: ranked group: main file + sidecars,\nexif, fingerprint
activate Validator

== validator ==

Validator -> DB: the main file's fingerprint\n(size + sha256 of its ends)
activate DB

alt found the same
    note over Validator, DB
    same path and same hash:
    only reached when the item is not done
    (the gate drops the rest)
    end note
    DB -> Validator: <font color=blue><b>existing guid

else found moved
    note over Validator, DB
    same hash, different path,
    old path <b><font color=red>not exists
    The item may be deleted already (deletions ran
    first: the chain is async) -> restored
    end note
    DB <- DB: update path, new file rows\ntake the item's GUID
    DB -> Validator: <font color=blue><b>existing guid
    note over Validator: goes on: the cheap stage refreshes\nthe preview path (it moved too)

else don't found
    note over Validator, DB
    path and hash not found
    create new item
    end note
    note over Validator, DB
    same hash, different path,
    old path <b><font color=red>also exists
    create new one (duplicate)
    end note
    DB <- DB: create
    DB -> Validator: <font color=green><b>new guid

else found changed
    note over Validator, DB
    same path, different hash
    <b>have to regenerate thumbs
    end note
    DB -> Validator: <font color=blue><b>existing guid</b></font>, Dirty
    deactivate DB
end

Validator -> Transcode: item (guid), group, exif
deactivate Validator
note over Transcode #LightGreen: then the exif step (perceptors); commit sets <b>Visible</b> or <b>Waiting</b>

== end of walk: the missing files ==

note over Groups, DB #LightGreen
The walk sends missing files only after a <b>complete</b> walk with files found
(not on cancel, missing root, empty root), after the files it saw.
Rows the walk did not see (read at its start), under the root,
not under an unreadable directory, are missing; their provider decides what is
gone for the library (Apple also counts the files of assets
trashed or hidden in Photos).
The gate has the model apply it:
- main file gone -> item <b>Deleted</b> (soft delete, hidden from /items)
- sidecar gone -> item <b>Dirty</b> (its group passes the gate again)
- file rows deleted
end note

@enduml
